1. Project Initialization & Dependencies
Node.js (Express)

Node.js me aap npm init karke package.json banate hain aur Express install karte hain:
Bash

mkdir node-api && cd node-api
npm init -y
npm install express

Axum (Rust)

Rust me project create karne ke liye Cargo (Rust ka package manager & build system) ka use hota hai:
Bash

cargo new axum-api
cd axum-api
cargo add axum@0.8 tokio -F tokio/full

    Fayda: cargo add automatically dependencies ko Cargo.toml me add karke download aur compile kar leta hai, bilkul npm install ki tarah. -F tokio/full ka matlab hai ki hum Tokio async runtime ke saare features enable kar rahe hain.

2. Code Breakdown (src/main.rs)

Rust me code hamesha main.fn se start hota hai. Yeh raha code aur iska har ek hissa Node.js se kaise milta-julta hai:
Rust

use axum::{Router, routing::get};

#[tokio::main]
async fn main() {
    // 1. Router define karna
    let app = Router::new().route("/", get(|| async { "Hello, World!" }));
 
    // 2. TCP listener bind karna port 3000 par
    let listener = tokio::net::TcpListener::bind("0.0.0.0:3000").await.unwrap();
    println!("Listening on http://localhost:3000");
    
    // 3. Server start karna
    axum::serve(listener, app).await.unwrap();
}

Key Concepts Comparison:

    #[tokio::main] Macro:

        Node.js: Event loop background me khud-ba-khud chalta hai.

        Rust: Rust me asynchronous code chalane ke liye ek async runtime ki zaroorat hoti hai. #[tokio::main] hamare synchronous main() function ko ek async Tokio runtime par run kar deta hai.

    Router::new().route(...):

        Node.js (Express): app.get('/', (req, res) => res.send('Hello'))

        Axum: Yahan get(...) ke andar ek inline async closure (|| async { ... }) pass kiya gaya hai jo bina kisi res.send() ke seedha string return kar raha hai. Axum khud samajh jata hai ki string ko HTTP response me kaise convert karna hai.

    TcpListener & axum::serve:

        Node.js (Express): app.listen(3000) sab kuch internally handle kar leta hai.

        Axum: Axum thoda low-level control deta hai. Pehle hum ek TCP socket bind karte hain (TcpListener), aur phir us listener par Axum server (axum::serve) chalaate hain.

3. Running and Testing

Server ko run karne ke liye terminal me run karein:
Bash

cargo run

(Yeh pehli baar compile hone me thoda waqt lega kyunki dependencies build ho rahi hain).

Dusre terminal me test karne ke liye:
Bash

curl http://localhost:3000
# Output => Hello, World!